From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:22:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: Don't walk into an absent level 1 page table

An unmap walk does not create page tables. When it loads a level 1
table that is absent, pvr_mmu_op_context_load_tables() leaves
curr_page.l1_table NULL and returns success. Removing the last level 0
table of a level 1 table also frees that level 1 table and clears
curr_page.l1_table. In both cases, the next page that crosses only a
level 0 boundary asks for a level 0 reload, and
pvr_page_table_l0_get_or_insert() reads the level 1 entry through the
NULL table:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000001008
  pc : pvr_mmu_op_context_load_tables+0xd8/0x1dc [powervr]
  lr : pvr_mmu_op_context_next_page+0xbc/0xd4 [powervr]
   pvr_mmu_op_context_unmap_curr_page+0x48/0x68 [powervr]
   pvr_mmu_unmap+0x2c/0x38 [powervr]

0x1008 is the backing page's host_ptr behind the 512-entry mirror
array. Unmapping a range only after it was mapped never reaches this,
but an unmap of a range that is already partly or fully unmapped does,
for example when restoring an evicted mapping first clears whatever an
interrupted eviction left behind.

Without a level 1 table there is no level 0 table either. Report
-ENXIO like any other absent table when not inserting, so the walk
treats the range as unmapped. A walk that inserts tables always loads
the level 1 table first, so warn if it ever gets here.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_mmu.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_mmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_mmu.c
index c9e89e1940..80d93cb1ad 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_mmu.c
@@ -1787,9 +1787,11 @@ pvr_page_table_l1_get_or_insert(struct pvr_mmu_op_context *op_ctx,
  *  * 0 on success,
  *
  *    If @should_insert is %false:
- *     * -%ENXIO if a level 0 page table would have been inserted.
+ *     * -%ENXIO if a level 0 page table would have been inserted, or if
+ *       there is no level 1 page table to look in.
  *
  *    If @should_insert is %true:
+ *     * -%EINVAL if there is no level 1 page table to insert into, or
  *     * Any error encountered while inserting the level 0 page table.
  */
 static int
@@ -1798,6 +1800,18 @@ pvr_page_table_l0_get_or_insert(struct pvr_mmu_op_context *op_ctx,
 {
 	struct pvr_page_table_l0 *table;
 
+	/*
+	 * A walk that does not create tables can reach a level 0 boundary with
+	 * no level 1 table: the level 1 table was absent when it was loaded,
+	 * or removing its last entry earlier in the same walk freed it. There
+	 * is then no level 0 table either.
+	 */
+	if (!op_ctx->curr_page.l1_table) {
+		if (WARN_ON_ONCE(should_insert))
+			return -EINVAL;
+		return -ENXIO;
+	}
+
 	if (pvr_page_table_l1_entry_is_valid(op_ctx->curr_page.l1_table,
 					     op_ctx->curr_page.l1_idx)) {
 		op_ctx->curr_page.l0_table =
